---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<!-- Starting draft — must be reviewed by a qualified professional before the site accepts real traffic. -->
{/*
  TODO — YOU MUST SET A REAL, WORKING EMAIL ADDRESS.

  Set SITE.author.email and SITE.legal.privacyEmail in src/config.ts. AdSense
  review checks that a genuine contact method exists and that it works — a
  placeholder address is a common reason for rejection. Send yourself a test
  message from a different account before applying.

  Also fill in a postal address below if you want one shown; it is not
  mandatory for AdSense, but it does help the site read as a real operation.
*/}

<PageLayout
  title="Contact"
  description={`How to reach a person at ${SITE.name} — corrections, questions, advertising and press.`}
  path="/contact"
  subtitle="Corrections, questions, advertising and press — all reach a person."
>
  <h2>Email</h2>

  <p>
    Email is the way to reach us, and a person reads everything that arrives. We reply
    to most messages within two to three working days.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>General, editorial and corrections</strong> —
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.author.email}`}>{SITE.author.email}</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Privacy, data and DPDP/GDPR requests</strong> —
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.legal.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.legal.privacyEmail}</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>

  <p>
    If an article contains a factual error, tell us which article and which specific
    claim is wrong, and link a source if you have one. Corrections are made promptly
    and the article's update date is changed so readers can see it has been revised.
    Given that our drafts are AI-assisted and human-reviewed, we take correction
    reports seriously — they are how the review process gets better.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>

  <p>
    Advertising on this site is sold through Google AdSense, not by us directly, so
    there is no media kit to request. We do not sell sponsored posts, paid editorial
    coverage, or links inside existing articles. If that is what you are looking for,
    we are not the right fit, and we would rather say so immediately than waste your
    time.
  </p>

  <h2>Press and product briefings</h2>

  <p>
    We are happy to receive product news, embargoed briefings and beta access. Doing so
    creates no obligation to cover anything, and no obligation to cover it favourably.
    Where a company has provided access or a review unit, we say so in the article.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>

  <p>
    We are a publication, not a support desk. We cannot recover your account, refund a
    purchase, or troubleshoot a product on behalf of the company that makes it —
    contact the vendor directly for any of those. We also do not provide personalised
    medical, legal, financial or tax advice; see the
    <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Postal address</h2>

  <p>
    {SITE.legal.entityName}<br />
    {SITE.legal.address}
  </p>
</PageLayout>
